{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b1c2d3e4-f5a6-7890-bcde-1234567890ab",
    "name": "Incubator Service",
    "description": "Postman collection for the incubator-service NestJS API.\n\n## Environment\n- **Incubator Local** — `http://localhost:3000`\n\n## Linear walkthrough (run folders top to bottom)\n1. **Testing** — reset the database\n2. **Users** — `POST /users` creates a login-ready (auto-confirmed) user and seeds `user_login`/`user_password`\n3. **Auth** — `POST /auth/login` captures `access_token`; sets the `refreshToken` cookie\n4. **Blogs** — captures `blog_id`, then `post_id` from the nested blog post\n5. **Posts** — captures `comment_id` from the post comment\n6. **Comments** — read/update the captured comment\n7. **Security** — list active devices (captures `device_id`)\n8. **Teardown** — `POST /auth/logout`\n\n**Optional** — registration flow, destructive DELETEs, logout-all. Not part of the walkthrough.\n\n### Caveats\n- Access token expires in **10s** and the refresh token in **20s** — run requests promptly or re-login/refresh.\n- The `refreshToken` cookie is `Secure` + `HttpOnly`. Postman's cookie jar carries it automatically; over plain `http://localhost` a Secure cookie may not persist, which can break refresh/logout/device requests. See postman/README.md.\n- `email` fields are validated as a **URL** (`@IsUrl`), so use values like `https://example.com/user123`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "if (!pm.environment.name) {",
          "    throw new Error('Select an environment first: Incubator Local');",
          "}",
          "const base = pm.environment.get('base_url');",
          "if (!base) {",
          "    throw new Error('base_url is not set in the environment');",
          "}",
          "if (base.endsWith('/')) {",
          "    pm.environment.set('base_url', base.replace(/\\/+$/, ''));",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
